  "query_preview": "..\nUpper ridging has flattened into a zonal flow regime across \neastern Montana and the Northern High Plains, bringing a brief\nreprieve from the highs in the upper 60s. \n\nA fast moving shortwave will eject out of the Pacific Northwest\nand over the Northern Rockies and into eastern Montana and Wyoming\novernight and Tuesday. This will likely result in increased cloud\ncover and perhaps a stray shower, though most ensembles suggest\nspotty coverage QPF and remaining mainly in southwest Montana.\n\nEnsembles show a large high amplitude upper ridge becoming\nestablished over the western CONUS for the second half of the week\nwhich will result in prominent dry weather conditions and warmer\ntemperatures as highs return to the 50s and 60s for much of NE\nMontana. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo deviation from the NBM.\n\nThere remains uncertainty with respect to just how quickly the \nridge is broken down, and the strength and location of the low \noff the coast of Baja California.",
